# WN22-DC-000060: Windows Server 2022 computer clock synchronization tolerance must be limited to five minutes or less.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-dc-000060-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 computer clock synchronization tolerance must be limited to five minutes or less.`
    description `This setting determines the maximum time difference (in minutes) that Kerberos will tolerate between the time on a client's clock and the time on a server's clock while still considering the two clocks synchronous. To prevent replay attacks, Kerberos uses timestamps as part of its protocol definition. For timestamps to work properly, the clocks of the client and the server need to be in sync as much as possible. Satisfies: SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057, SRG-OS-000113-GPOS-00058`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,kerberos-policy,security-policy,ksi-iam-apm,ksi-iam-mfa`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-APM,KSI:KSI-IAM-MFA,NIST-800-53:IA-2(8)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-APM,KSI-IAM-MFA`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value in the Default Domain Policy for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Account Policies >> Kerberos Policy >> Maximum tolerance for computer clock synchronization to a maximum of "5" minutes or less.`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_IAM_APM `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-APM by enforcing MaxClockSkew per the STIG (Computer clock synchronization tolerance must be <= 5 minutes.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_MFA `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-MFA by enforcing MaxClockSkew per the STIG (Computer clock synchronization tolerance must be <= 5 minutes.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_IA_2_8 `Windows Server implements IA-2(8) by enforcing MaxClockSkew per the STIG (Computer clock synchronization tolerance must be <= 5 minutes.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `MaxClockSkew`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int <= 5
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
